title: $:/plugins/rimir/mindmap/producers
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

! Producers

A ''producer'' is a `module-type: mindmap-producer` JS module that turns wiki data into a base MDOM document. Built-in producers cover the common cases; custom producers can be added in any plugin that registers a module of this type.

!! Built-in producers

!!! filter-tree

Title-path segmentation of any filter result.

|!Argument |!Default |!Purpose |
|`filter` |(required) |TW filter expression returning titles to include |
|`delimiter` |`/` |Path separator used for tree segmentation |
|`root-label` |`Mindmap` |Label for the synthetic root |
|`body-field` |`text` |Tiddler field shown as MDOM node body |

Used implicitly by the `<$mindmap filter="..."/>` quick form. Node IDs are prefixed `ft:`.

!!! knowledge-tree

Renders a `rimir/knowledge-app` area as a mindmap. Enriches nodes with type icons (from `kn.type`) and area colour.

|!Argument |!Default |!Purpose |
|`area` |(required) |Area id (e.g. `llm`, `health`) |
|`delimiter` |`/` |Path separator |
|`include-areas-root` |`no` |If `yes`, renders a forest of all areas (ignores `area`) |

Node IDs are prefixed `kt:`.

!!! json

Reads MDOM verbatim from a tiddler's text field.

|!Argument |!Default |!Purpose |
|`tiddler` |(required) |Title of a tiddler whose text is valid MDOM JSON |

!! Installed producers (all sources)

<$list filter="[mindmap-producers[]]">
* <<currentTiddler>>
</$list>

!! Writing a custom producer

Create a JS module with header:

```
title: $:/your-plugin/producers/my-producer.js
type: application/javascript
module-type: mindmap-producer
```

Export the following:

```
exports.name = "my-producer";
exports.produce = function (args, wiki) {
    return {
        version: 1,
        root: { id: "mine:root", label: "...", children: [...] },
        meta: { producer: "my-producer", producedAt: Date.now() }
    };
};
exports.refreshFilter = function (args) {
    return "[your-filter-here]";   // optional; widget re-projects when matching tiddlers change
};
exports.describe = function () {
    return { name: "my-producer", args: [...] };
};
```

Node IDs SHOULD be stable across renders and prefixed with a namespace unique to your producer.
